# port-patches.sh: glm/r8b @ cf4dde927470 over glm/zig-engine-fixes-on-186 @ e027c49cd06d (commits f190863a4e08..6cc5c62a69ae); regenerate with scripts/port-patches.sh, do not edit
glm_cuda: the ranks agree on TF_GLM_NUCLEUS_RACE with TENSORFOLD_NUCLEUS_UNION (one word, bit 1)

The race, like the union test, changes which collectives a draw issues; a rank with it off would wait on a different
second gather. Both go in the one word the ranks already exchange at start.

Credits: Robert Wojciechowski (GitHub @wojo, X @rwojo).
Apply from the checkout root with: git apply 0036-zig-glm-nucleus-agree.patch

diff --git a/zig/src/families/glm_cuda/cuda_engine.zig b/zig/src/families/glm_cuda/cuda_engine.zig
index 88f48947b87318d37bece874c961ccbc3d848f19..604b69ae28a46e14f4aa2ef5ae03557751840d83 100644
